   "text": {
    "L1": "India became home to many communities over many centuries.",
    "L2": "Some came for trade, and others came seeking safety to practise their faith.",
    "L3": "Many arrived by sea at busy west-coast ports, helped by the monsoon winds.",
    "L4": "Local rulers often welcomed them and gave some communities rights and privileges.",
    "L5": "The newcomers kept their faith, while adopting local languages, dress and food.",
    "L6": "Parsis settled at Sanjan, and Kerala's Jews and Christians became part of local life.",
    "L7": "Their businesses, foods, buildings and knowledge enriched India's culture.",
    "L8": "That is why India is a home to many: communities live and work together."
   },
